# --- Line-ending policy (wtp-org#992 pattern 7) ------------------------------
# Store every text file as LF and check it out as LF on every OS, so Windows
# clones (core.autocrlf=true by default) stop producing CRLF churn, broken
# shebangs, and platform-dependent hashes. Rules further down this file are
# more specific and take precedence over this catch-all.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts need CRLF in the working tree (cmd.exe requires it for
# .cmd/.bat; keep .ps1 consistent with Windows tooling). Stored as LF in git.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf
*.psd1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary files — never normalise or diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
